quran[6]{c,v,t}:
  57,19,"And those who believe in Allah and His messengers, it is they who are truthful and are witnesses before their Lord. They shall have their reward and their light. But those who disbelieve and reject Our Signs—they shall be the inmates of the Hellfire."
  57,20,"Know that the life of this world is only play, diversion, glamour, mutual boasting and competition for increasing wealth and children. (It is) like the rain (that causes plants to grow), whose vegetation impresses the farmers. Then it withers, and you see it turning yellow, and then it becomes bits of trash. And in the Hereafter, there will be severe punishment or forgiveness from Allah and (His) great pleasure. And the life of this world is nothing but the enjoyment of delusion."
  57,21,"So race towards forgiveness from your Lord and Paradise, as vast as the heavens and the earth. (It is) prepared for those who believe in Allah and His messengers. That is Allah’s grace, which He grants to whomsoever He pleases. And Allah is the Possessor of the Tremendous Grace."
  57,22,"No calamity befalls the earth or yourselves, but it is (recorded) in a Book before We make it happen. Indeed, that is easy for Allah."
  57,23,(It is) so that you may not grieve for what has escaped you nor boast for what has come to you. And Allah does not like whoever is arrogant (and) boastful.
  57,24,"(Such as) those who are miserly (themselves) and tell (other) people to be miserly. And whosoever turns away (from Allah’s injunctions should know that) Allah is indeed the All-Sufficient, the All-Praised."
